mutate_grid.py output. THREE passes, in the order they were run. The FINAL pass (section C) is the one that stands: every mutant against the final 127-test file.
Run as two parallel parts (`--part k/2`) in two identical copies of the tree; the harness applies one anchored byte-replacement at a time, restores it in a `finally`, and asserts byte-identical restoration.
Mutants are tried on their own group's tests first (`-k`); a mutant that survives them is tried against the WHOLE file before it is called GREEN (a survivor).

